# CLI Extensions

This document describes extension methods for easy CLI service setup and usage.

**Location:** `Extensions/CliServiceExtensions.cs`

```csharp
namespace Cyrena.CLI.Extensions;

public static class CliServiceExtensions
{
    public static CliService Create(Action<CliService>? configure = null);
    public static CliService RegisterFromCurrentAssembly(this CliService service);
    public static CliService RegisterFromAssembly(this CliService service, Assembly assembly);
    public static CliService RegisterFromType<T>(this CliService service, T? instance = null) where T : class;
    public static CliExecutionResult ParseAndExecute(this CliService service, string[] args);
    public static bool ParseAndExecuteWithExit(this CliService service, string[] args);
}
```

## Methods

### Create

Creates and optionally configures a new CliService instance.

```csharp
public static CliService Create(Action<CliService>? configure = null);
```

**Usage:**
```csharp
var service = CliServiceExtensions.Create(s => 
{
    s.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();
});
```

### RegisterFromCurrentAssembly

Registers all CLI commands from the calling assembly.

```csharp
public static CliService RegisterFromCurrentAssembly(this CliService service);
```

**Usage:**
```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();
```

### RegisterFromAssembly

Registers all CLI commands from a specified assembly.

```csharp
public static CliService RegisterFromAssembly(this CliService service, Assembly assembly);
```

**Usage:**
```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromAssembly(typeof(SomeCommands).Assembly);
```

### RegisterFromType

Registers all CLI commands from a specific type.

```csharp
public static CliService RegisterFromType<T>(this CliService service, T? instance = null) where T : class;
```

**Usage:**
```csharp
// With auto-created instance
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromType<SomeCommands>();

// With custom instance (for dependency injection scenarios)
var commands = new SomeCommands(dependency1, dependency2);
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromType(commands);
```

### ParseAndExecute

Parses command-line arguments and executes the appropriate command. Returns a result indicating whether the application should continue booting.

```csharp
public static CliExecutionResult ParseAndExecute(this CliService service, string[] args);
```

**Returns:** `CliExecutionResult` with boot flow information.

**Behavior:**
- If `args` is empty, returns `NoCommand()` → application should continue booting
- If a command is executed successfully, returns `CommandExecuted()` → application should exit
- If help is displayed, returns `CommandExecuted()` → application should exit
- If an unknown command is specified, returns `UnknownCommand()` → application should exit with error

**Usage:**
```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();

var result = service.ParseAndExecute(args);

if (!result.ShouldContinueBoot)
{
    // CLI command was handled, exit the application
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Message))
    {
        Console.WriteLine(result.Message);
    }
    return result.ExitCode ?? 0;
}

// No command specified, continue with normal application boot
Console.WriteLine("Starting application...");
```

### ParseAndExecuteWithExit

Parses and executes CLI commands, automatically exiting the application if a command was executed.

```csharp
public static bool ParseAndExecuteWithExit(this CliService service, string[] args);
```

**Returns:** `true` if the application should continue booting (only returned if no command was specified).

**Behavior:**
- If a command was executed or help was shown, calls `Environment.Exit()` and never returns
- If no command was specified, returns `true` to continue boot

**Usage:**
```csharp
var service = new CliService();
service.RegisterFromCurrentAssembly();

// This will exit the app if a command was executed
service.ParseAndExecuteWithExit(args);

// Only reached if no command was specified
Console.WriteLine("Starting application...");
```

## Complete Example

### Program.cs Pattern

```csharp
using Cyrena.CLI.Extensions;
using Cyrena.CLI.Attributes;

namespace MyApp.CLI.Services;

public class ConfigCommands
{
    [CliCommand("configure", Description = "Configures application settings")]
    public void Configure(
        [CliParam("setting", Required = true, Description = "Setting name")] string setting,
        [CliParam("value", Required = true, Description = "Setting value")] string value
    )
    {
        // Save configuration
        Console.WriteLine($"Configured {setting}={value}");
    }
}

// In Program.cs
var service = CliServiceExtensions.Create(s => 
    s.RegisterFromType<ConfigCommands>()
);

var result = service.ParseAndExecute(args);

if (!result.ShouldContinueBoot)
{
    // Command was executed, exit application
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(result.Message))
    {
        Console.WriteLine(result.Message);
    }
    return result.ExitCode ?? 0;
}

// No command specified, start the main application
Console.WriteLine("Starting background service...");
// ... rest of application initialization
```

### Command-Line Scenarios

| Command | Result | Behavior |
|---------|--------|----------|
| `./MyApp` | Continue | Application boots normally |
| `./MyApp configure --setting=x --value=y` | Stop (0) | Configures, then exits |
| `./MyApp help` | Stop (0) | Shows help, then exits |
| `./MyApp unknown` | Stop (1) | Shows error, then exits |
